Z||000008||DaRkLoRD||04-23-2000||09:54 PM||||I wasn't being sarcastic, I was serious.. I guess it does sound like a silly explanation tho, but doesn't referring to a car as an 86.5 model also sound a bit strange? If they didn't release the fastback GT until part way through 1986, what were they doing the first half of that year?<P>anyway, I don't know a lot about this, it's all just speculation on my part. When I said an 85 GT that was made in 86.. I should have just said a notchback GT.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||batboy||04-23-2000||09:54 PM||||Last summer I made a statement that 85 was the only year for a GT notchback and was "corrected" by a couple folks that heard of early 86 notchback GT's.<P>I felt dumb at the time, but I'm beginning to think it's an urban legend. I might write a story about the notchback 86 Fiero GT like that guy did about the rocket car.<P>I have yet to see a documented 86 GT that is a notchback. Doesn't mean they don't exist. But, everytime I hear about one it's a friend's uncle's boss had one, or something like that.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Raydar||04-24-2000||12:51 AM||||FWIW... I bought an 85 GT, new. (Yeah, I'm an old fart.) Shortly after, I started hearing rumors of a 5 speed (Getrag) in the works, for the 86 model year. Went back to the dealer on a regular basis, after the 86 models came out. Pretty much made a pest of myself. Saw a *bunch* of notchback aero SE's, but didn't see a single GT until the fastbacks were released. Just my $.02<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 04-24-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||fieroshop||04-24-2000||01:39 AM||||GM knew they were coming out with a new GT in 86, so they named all 85 GT's SE's If you look closely you will find no difference in the way the SE" and the 85 GT look. They did continue with the same design in 87.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Standard||04-24-2000||03:09 AM||||There are no 86 GT notchbacks... when someone is talking about an 86.5 GT they're talking about the 5 speed getrag, which was a mid-late year switchover for the 86 GT.  only around 2200 made.. and I got one!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>sfaik, the only difference between the GT and SE models (other than the fastback) is that the GT had more standard options.  ||||reg||1
